  "about": "A portable ADS-B receiver's GDL 90 stream over Wi-Fi (Garmin's GDL 90 Data Interface Specification 560-1058-00 Rev A; ForeFlight's ID message), read by the engine's receiver_read and the views over it (receiver_traffic, receiver_reports, receiver_nexrad). Two datagrams a second apart, built by engine/crates/receiver/tests/stream.rs: the specification's own Heartbeat (2.2.4) and Traffic Report (3.5.4, N825V), a Sentry's ID message, own ship N12345 near O'Hare at 3,000 ft pressure altitude and 3,200 ft MSL by GPS, and an uplink from a station at 41.9 N 87.9 W with O'Hare's METAR and TAF (FIS-B product 413), a TFR's text (product 8) and one regional NEXRAD block (product 63), then a damaged frame. Expected values are the specification's and the built products', not the engine's.",
